{
  "title": "Dua-e-Sayfee Sagheer (Dua Qaamoos)",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ \nBISMILLAHIR RAHMANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah; the All-beneficent, the All-merciful \nرَبِّ اَدْخِلْنِيْ فِيْ لُجَّةِ بَحْرِ اَحَدِيَّتِكَ \nRABBE ADKHILNEE FEE LUJJATE BAHRE AHADIYYATEKA \nO my Lord, include me with the profundity of the ocean of Your Oneness \nوَ طَمْطَامِ يَمِّ وَحْدَانِيَّتِكَ \nWA TAMTAAME YAMME WAHDAANIYYATEKA \nand in the enormity of the sea of Your singleness. \nوَ قَوِّنِىْ بِقُوَّةِ سَطْوَةِ سُلْطَانِ فَرْدَانِيَّتِكَ \nWA QAWWENEE BE-QUWWATE SATWATE SULTAANE FARDAANIYYATEKA \nStrengthen me with the strength of the influence of the authority of Your Uniqueness \nحَتّٰى اَخْرُجَ اِلٰى فَضَاۤءِ سَعَةِ رَحْمَتِكَ \nHATTAA AKHROJA ELAA FAZAAA-E SA-A'TE RAHMATEKA \nso that when I come out to the space of the breadth of Your mercy, \nوَ فِيْ وَجْهِيْ لَمَعَاتُ بَرْقِ الْقُرْبِ مِنْ اٰثَارِ حِمَايَتِكَ \nWA FEE WAJHEE LAMA-A'ATO BARQIL QURBE MIN AASAARE HEMAAYATEKA \nmy face will have the twinkles of the shining of the nearness to the traces of Your protection, \nمَهِيْبًا بِهَيْبَتِكَ عَزِيْزًا بِعِنَايَتِكَ \nMAHEEBAN BE-HAYBATEKA A'ZEEZAN BE-E'NAAYATEKA \nbeing venerable out of Your venerability, mighty out of Your care (for me), \nمُتَجَلِّلًا مُكَرَّمًا بِتَعْلِيْمِكَ وَ تَزْكِيَتِكَ \nMOTAJALLELAN MOKARRAMAN BE-TA'LEEMEKA WA TAZKIYYATEKA \nesteemed, and honored out of Your instruction and purity. \nوَ اَلْبِسْنِيْ خِلَعَ الْعِزَّةِ وَ الْقَبُوْلِ \nWA ALBISNEE KHELA-A'L I'ZZATE WAL QABOOLE \nDress me with the garments of dignity and tolerability, \nوَ سَهِّلْ لِيْ مَنَاهِجَ الْوُصْلَةِ وَ الْوُصُوْلِ \nWA SAHHIL LEE MANAAHEJAL WUSLATE WAL WOSOOLE \nmake easy for me to attain the courses of communication and attainment (to You), \nوَ تَوِّجْنِيْ بِتَاجِ الْكَرَامَةِ وَ الْوَقَارِ \nWA TAWWIJNEE BE-TAAJIL KARAAMATE WAL WAQAARE \nadorn me with the crown of decorum and solemnity, \nوَ اَلِّفْ بَيْنِيْ وَ بَيْنَ اَحِبَّاۤئِكَ فِيْ دَارِ الدُّنْيَا وَ دَارِ الْقَرَارِ \nWA ALLIF BAYNEE WA BAYNA AHIBBAAA-EKA FEE DAARID DUNYAA WA DAARIL QARAARE \nand put affection between your beloved ones and me in this worldly abode as well as the Abode of Enduring Settlement. \nوَ ارْزُقْنِيْ مِنْ نُوْرِ اسْمِكَ هَيْبَةً \nWAR ZUQNEE MIN NOORIS MEKA HAYBATAN \nOut of the illumination of Your Name, \nوَ سَطْوَةً تَنْقَادُ لِيَ الْقُلُوْبُ وَ الْاَرْوَاحُ \nWA SATWATAN TANQAADO LEYAL QOLOOBO WAL ARWAAHO \nconfer upon me with honor and authority due to which all hearts and souls will submit to me, \nوَ تَخْضَعُ لَدَيَّ النُّفُوْسُ وَ الْاَشْبَاحُ \nWA TAKHZA-O' LADAYYAN NOFOOSO WAL ASHBAAHO \nand all selves and ghosts will succumb to me. \nيَا مَنْ ذَلَّتْ لَهٗ رِقَابُ الْجَبَابِرَةِ \nYAA MAN ZALLAT LAHU REQAABUL JABAABERATE \nO He to Whom all the tyrants surrender, \nوَ خَضَعَتْ لَدَيْهِ اَعْنَاقُ الْاَكَاسِرَةِ \nWA KHAZA-A'T LADAYHE A-A'NAAQUL AKAASERATE \nand before Whom all the kings submit! \nلَا مَلْجَاَ وَ لَا مَنْجٰى مِنْكَ اِلَّا اِلَيْكَ \nLAA MALJAA WA LAA MANJAA MINKA ILLAA ELAYKA \nThere in neither shelter nor refuge (to protect) against You save to You, \nوَ لَاۤ اِعَانَةَ اِلَّا بِكَ وَ لَاۤ اتِّكَاۤءَ اِلَّا عَلَيْكَ \nWA LAA E-A'ANATA ILLAA BEKA WA LAT-TEKAA-A ILLAA A'LAYKAD \nthere is no help save through You, and there is no reliance save upon You. \nادْفَعْ عَنِّيْ كَيْدَ الْحَاسِدِيْنَ\nFA' A'NNEE KAYDAL HAASEDEENA.\nRepel against me the trickeries of the envious ones \nوَ ظُلُمَاتِ شَرِّ الْمُعَانِدِيْنَ \nWA ZOLOMAATE SHARRIL MO-A'ANEDEENA \nand the murk of the evils of the stubborn ones. \nوَ ارْحَمْنِيْ تَحْتَ سُرَادِقَاتِ عَرْشِكَ \nWAR HAMNEE TAHTA SORAADEQAATE A'RSHEKA \nHave mercy upon me under the pavilion of Your Throne; \nيَا اَكْرَمَ الْاَكْرَمِيْنَ \nYAA AKRAMAL AKRAMEENA \nO most Generous of all those who show generosity! \nاَيِّدْ ظَاهِرِيْ فِيْ تَحْصِيْلِ مَرَاضِيْكَ \nAYYID ZAAHEREE FEE TAHSEELE MARAAZEEKA \nAid my appearance to attain Your pleasure \nوَ نَوِّرْ قَلْبِيْ وَ سِرِّيْ بِالْاِطِّلَاعِ عَلٰى مَنَاهِجِ مَسَاعِيْكَ \nWA NAWWIR QALBEE WA SIRREE BIL-ITTELAA-E' A'LAA MANAAHEJE MASAA-E'EKA \nand illuminate my heart and inner self by making me acquainted with the courses to acting for Your sake. \nاِلٰهِيْ كَيْفَ اَصْدُرُ عَنْ بَابِكَ بِخَيْبَةٍ مِّنْكَ \nELAAHEE KAYFA ASDORO A'N BAABEKA BE-KHAYBATIM MINKA \nO my God, how does it come that I leave Your Door with disappointment \nوَ قَدْ وَرَدْتُهٗ عَلٰى ثِقَةٍ بِكَ \nWA QAD WARADTOHU A'LAA SEQATIN BEKA \nafter I had come to it with full faith in You? \nوَ كَيْفَ تُؤْيِسُنِيْ مِنْ عَطَاۤئِكَ \nWA KAYFA TOA-YESONEE MIN A'TAAA-EKA \nHow is it possible that You drive me to despair of Your endowment \nوَ قَدْ اَمَرْتَنِيْ بِدُعَاۤئِكَ \nWA QAD AMARTANEE BEDO-A'AA-EKA \nafter You have instructed me to pray to You? \nوَ هَا اَنَا مُقْبِلٌ عَلَيْكَ مُلْتَجِئٌ اِلَيْكَ \nWA HAA ANAA MUQBELUN A'LAYKA MULTA-JE-UN ELAYKA \nHere I am coming to You seeking shelter with You. \nبَاعِدْ بَيْنِيْ وَ بَيْنَ اَعْدَاۤئِىْ \nBAA-I'D BAYNEE WA BAYNA A-A'DAA-EE \nKeep me far away from my enemies \nكَمَا بَاعَدْتَ بَيْنَ اَعْدَاۤئِىْ\nKAMAA BAA-A'DTA BAYNA A-A'DAA-EE \njust as You have kept my enemies far away from one another. \nاِخْتَطِفْ اَبْصَارَهُمْ عَنِّيْ بِنُوْرِ قُدْسِكَ \nIKHTATIF ABSAARAHUM A'NNEE BE-NOORE QUDSEKA \nTake their sights away from me through the Light of Your Holiness \nوَ جَلَالِ مَجْدِكَ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ اللهُ الْمُعْطِىْ \nWA JALAALE MAJDEKA INNAKA ANTAL LAAHUL MO'TEE \nand the Grandeur of Your Glory. You are verily Allah Who confers \nجَلَاۤئِلَ النِّعَمِ الْمُكَرَّمَةِ \nJALAA-ELIN NE-A'MIL MOKARRAMATE \nwith the splendid honoring graces \nلِمَنْ نَاجَاكَ بِلَطَاۤئِفِ رَحْمَتِكَ \nLEMAN NAAJAAKA BE-LATAA-EFE RAHMATEKA \nupon those who secretly pray to You out of Your tremendous mercy. \nيَا حَىُّ يَا قَيُّوْمُ يَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَ الْاِكْرَامِ \nYAA HAYYO YAA QAYYOOMO YAA ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAME \nO Ever-living, O Self-subsisting, O Lord of Glory and Honor! \nوَ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلٰى سَيِّدِنَا وَ نَبِيِّنَا مُحَمَّدٍ \nWA SALLAL LAAHO A'LAA SAYYEDENAA WA NABIYYENAA MOHAMMADINW\nMay Allah .send blessings to our master and Prophet, Muhammad, \nوَّ اٰلِهٖ اَجْمَعِيْنَ الطَّيِّبِيْنَ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ.\nWA AALEHI AJMA-E'ENAT TAYYEBEENAT TAAHEREEN.\nand upon all of his Household—the purified and immaculate.",
  "merits": "Also called Dua al-Qamus (The Supplicatory prayer of the Ocean), the trustworthy, noble Shaykh Mirza al-Nuri - may Allah honor his tomb - has mentioned this supplicatory prayer in his book entitled al-Sahifah al-Alawiyyah II, adding, “This supplication has been explained by the master scholars of talismans and spiritual sciences with strange words referring to marvelous effects ensuing from reciting it.”"
}
